================================================================================
THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
================================================================================

The MIT licence above covers CleanSplit's own code. The following directories
contain third-party code under their own licences, which are NOT MIT and which
govern those files. Each retains its upstream licence text.

  cleansplit/separation/bs_roformer/    MIT  — ZFTurbo/Music-Source-Separation-Training
  cleansplit/separation/mdx23c/         MIT  — ZFTurbo/Music-Source-Separation-Training
  cleansplit/separation/scnet/          MIT  — ZFTurbo/Music-Source-Separation-Training
                                        (all three: LICENSE_MSST.txt in bs_roformer/)
  cleansplit/ui/static/vendor/          BSD-3-Clause — wavesurfer.js, katspaugh and
                                        contributors (LICENSE_wavesurfer.txt)
  third_party/apollo/                   CC BY-SA 4.0 — Kai Li (JusperLee), Apollo
                                        (LICENSE in that directory)

third_party/apollo/ is a SHARE-ALIKE licence and deserves a plain statement
rather than a footnote: those files are licensed CC BY-SA 4.0, not MIT, and two
of them carry small documented modifications (see the header of apollo.py), so
those modified files remain CC BY-SA 4.0. CleanSplit's own code merely imports
them; it is not a derivative of them. Anyone redistributing this repository must
keep that directory under CC BY-SA 4.0. If that is unacceptable for your use,
delete third_party/apollo/ — the Apollo restorer is disabled by default and was
measured to be worse than doing nothing in 24 of 24 comparisons
(docs/04_results.md section 9), so nothing of value is lost.

MODEL WEIGHTS ARE NOT PART OF THIS REPOSITORY and are not redistributed. They
carry their own terms, which range from MIT (SCNet XL IHF) through
CC BY-NC (A2SB, MuScriptor: non-commercial only) to no explicit licence at all
(the UVR community checkpoints, including BS-RoFormer SW and ep317).
cleansplit/models/checkpoints.py records the licence note for each one.
